+# Focused native drawing registration — 2026-11-13
+
+## 🧭 Decision, complete scope and sequencing
+
+**Date/status/source:** 2026-11-13, accepted agent delivery-manager judgment under
+the owner's continuous backlog instruction and [standing decision authority](../todo/process.md#decisions).
+This is focused registration, not a full grooming, implementation, repaired gate
+or completed product ticket.
+
+**Question and options:** selected validation of the resumed SPN-120 found a native
+drawing interaction failure outside its finite historical fixture inventory.
+Treating a green variant or unchanged retry as acceptance, assigning it to unrelated
+SPN-087 CSS cleanup, or hiding it inside SPN-120 would lose that boundary. Register
+one complete **M, pre-launch** investigation/repair, SPN-159, and keep SPN-120 open
+with explicit prerequisites SPN-158 and SPN-159. The former owns the separately
+observed postcommit admission readiness HTTP 503; the latter owns native drawing
+resize observation and its full interaction/pending-mutation contract.
+
+SPN-159 retains diagnosis before repair, a predeclared bounded source/native
+experiment, meaningful phase/geometry observations, missing-transition negative
+controls, actual native insertion/selection/control refresh, original budgets,
+privacy, cleanup and all existing five Storybook variants. Its exact historical
+assertion and cause remain unknown. Establish the causal transition/readiness
+boundary through a predeclared new controlled experiment before choosing a repair;
+this does not require reconstructing the unavailable original failure phase.
+Reassess before expanding into a broader
+product/native-engine issue. SPN-120's L outcome and original finite cases remain
+intact; no product acceptance is removed to improve a grade.
+
+Operator gains visible work ownership and reliable gate evidence. Owner and
+Collaborator keep authored native changes distinct from UI-only resize/selection
+activity and retain SPN-120's data/access checks. Link guest retains native
+interaction and permission boundaries without gaining content or management
+access. Separate registration permits the investigation to proceed while retaining
+every failed gate and the cost of its complete verification.
+
+## 🧾 Allocation and preserved backlog state
+
+Preparation starts from independently verified actual main
+`89e4426dfff1c3469b260305e21180ffd79fdb7f`, next ID 159. No SPN-159 ticket path
+exists in the available Git history. The existing completed registration PR #284,
+its clean detached checkout, validation/completion archive tags and all prior
+ticket identities are preserved unchanged.
+
+Exactly one allocation ran through `npm run backlog:new -- 📐 "Observe completed
+native drawing resizes"`, advancing 159 to **160**. It passed under pinned Node
+26.13.0, the shared serial runner and runtime memory watchdog in **281 ms**, peak
+**160,672 KiB**, with normal pressure and no resource abort. The exact allocation
+commit remains in this branch's history; no ID was reused or manually allocated.
+
+No ticket is deleted or appended as completed. Preserve the current main's
+grooming date and completion list, and regenerate the index through the CLI.
+At the initial base these are **2026-11-12** and **[SPN-148, SPN-145]**. The manager
+plans publication after the already validating SPN-149 PR if its acceptance passes,
+to avoid invalidating near-ready CI. Before publication, integrate the actual new
+main, preserve any newly landed completion, run the relevant checks and obtain
+both independent exact-head reviews. That initial sequencing has now completed: SPN-149 landed in actual main
+`a3dfc6f3373babecf979d5b851bbbf46c6dbb3b9`, which this registration integrates.
+Its ticket removal and completion list **[SPN-148, SPN-145, SPN-149]** remain
+intact; last full grooming remains **2026-11-12**, with next ID **160**. The sole
+generated-index merge conflict was resolved by running the index CLI, not editing
+the generated file. This registration completes no product ticket.
+
+## 🔎 First failure, investigation limits and checks
+
+The [SPN-159 canonical record](SPN-159.md#-retained-failure-and-source-limits)
+retains source 47bf4aad, base 89e4426d, Storybook run 43554616505 attempt 1,
+desktop-light job 132324964897, artifact 14097504548 and its exact ZIP hash.
+The recorded counter error does not identify one of the three possible assertion
+sites. Post-failure full-width geometry does not diagnose an earlier transition.
+The source/main story hashes match, while the native source/runner contribution
+remains an investigation question. No native experiment or rerun is performed by
+this documentation PR. The [immutable failed-validation archive](https://github.com/mxbaylee/spinel/blob/4bd84e3be7645a3b18c794c966e0007e6770cc9c/docs/review-assets/spn-120-validation-47bf4aad/README.md)
+is now published at verified commit `4bd84e3be7645a3b18c794c966e0007e6770cc9c`;
+the original failed attempt remains visible and is not replaced by a retry.
+
+The complete open-PR listing during preparation returned **13 PRs**, all authored
+by `mxbaylee`: 220, 223, 224, 227, 228, 229, 230, 246, 247, 260, 281, 282 and 285.
+There are **no open Dependabot PRs** requiring security, compatibility, current-CI
+or grouping disposition. No dependency was changed or merged. Recheck this audit
+at the final publication base rather than treating this snapshot as permanent.
+The refreshed audit after integrating a3dfc6f3 returned **12 open PRs**, the same
+list excluding merged #282, all authored by `mxbaylee`; no Dependabot disposition
+is outstanding.
+
+Documentation verification owns allocation/history, exact heading, scope/persona
+rationale, dependency and phase ordering, evidence limits, local/immutable links,
+generated index and PR title/size rules. No application or UI implementation is
+changed. Product tests or routine new screenshots are not invented for registration;
+the existing failure screenshot is diagnostic provenance, not approval of a design.
+
+The initial generated-index check passed in **278 ms**, peak **215,792 KiB**;
+`backlog:check` passed for **31 open tickets** in **274 ms**, peak **212,496 KiB**,
+with only existing ticket-length guidance. Both used the pinned Node, shared serial
+runner and watchdog with normal pressure and no abort. `git diff --check` and
+local Markdown file-target resolution passed. The exact-head PR checker, final
+base integration and two independent reviews remain pending; these documentation
+checks are not native repair acceptance.
+
+After main integration, the index CLI passed in **172 ms** and `backlog:check`
+passed for **30 open tickets** in **149 ms**, with ticket-length guidance only.
+Both finished before the watchdog's first memory sample, so no measured peak
+is available; both passed normal-pressure preflight and had no resource abort.
+An earlier index invocation used a nonexistent `scripts/backlog.ts` path and
+failed before performing backlog work. Correcting it to the package script's
+`scripts/backlog/cli.ts index` produced the successful result above; retain both
+receipts rather than reporting the failed invocation as a pass. Final exact-head
+PR validation and independent reviews remain separate publication requirements.
